-- title:
--   Finite free algebras inherit adic completeness
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $I \subseteq \mathcal O$ an ideal such that $\mathcal O$ is $I$-adically complete in the sense of Mathlib's `IsAdicComplete`, that is, $\mathcal O$ is $I$-adically Hausdorff (an element lying in $I^n$ for every $n$ is zero) and $I$-adically precomplete (every sequence $(a_n)$ with $a_m \equiv a_n \bmod I^n$ for all $m \ge n$ has a limit $a$ with $a \equiv a_n \bmod I^n$ for all $n$). Let $R$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure such that $R$ is finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module. Then $R$ is adically complete for the ideal $I \cdot R =$ `I.map (algebraMap 𝓞 R)`, the ideal of $R$ generated by the image of $I$: $R$ is Hausdorff and precomplete for the filtration by the powers of that ideal. No local, Noetherian or finite-rank-uniformity assumption beyond freeness and finiteness of $R$ over $\mathcal O$ is imposed, and the ideal $I$ is arbitrary.
--
--   This is the standard fact that adic completeness ascends along a module-finite free base change, the $I \cdot R$-adic filtration of $R$ being the $I$-adic filtration of the $\mathcal O$-module $R \cong \mathcal O^n$. It is used to equip algebras of the form $\mathcal O[X]/(f)$ with $f$ monic with adic completeness, and is cited in the construction of étale extensions of complete local rings realising a prescribed residue field extension ([`AdjoinRoot.exists_isLocalRing_etale_residueField_algEquiv_of_isAdicComplete`](thm.html#AdjoinRoot.exists_isLocalRing_etale_residueField_algEquiv_of_isAdicComplete)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsAdicComplete_of_module_finite_free_map.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

theorem IsAdicComplete.of_module_finite_free_map
    {𝓞 : Type u} [CommRing 𝓞] (I : Ideal 𝓞) [IsAdicComplete I 𝓞]
    (R : Type v) [CommRing R] [Algebra 𝓞 R] [Module.Finite 𝓞 R] [Module.Free 𝓞 R] :
    IsAdicComplete (I.map (algebraMap 𝓞 R)) R := by sorry
